{"title":"Vote on the 2025 Tiny Awards Finalists","link":"https://waxy.org/2025/08/vote-on-the-2025-tiny-awards-finalists/","date":1754692719000,"content":"<p>For the third year, the <a href=\"https://tinyawards.net/\">Tiny Awards</a> have released their list of finalists that represent “the best of the small, poetic, creative, handmade web.” <a href=\"https://tinyawards.net/vote/\">Voting is now open</a> and runs until the end of this month, closing on September 1.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://tinyawards.net/vote/\"><img width=\"1024\" height=\"625\" src=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-12-1024x625.png\" srcset=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-12-1024x625.png 1024w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-12-300x183.png 300w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-12-768x468.png 768w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-12-1536x937.png 1536w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-12-2048x1249.png 2048w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-12-800x488.png 800w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>I was on the judging committee this year, returning after a year away to focus on <a href=\"https://waxy.org/2024/10/the-xoxo-2024-talks/\">the final XOXO</a>, and helped narrow down the finalists from 176 nominated websites.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>I love this little low-stakes contest, and the experience of being bombarded with so many great weird experimental projects is an honor for me.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Like my roundup <a href=\"https://waxy.org/2023/07/vote-on-the-tiny-awards/\">two years ago</a>, here’s a little about each of this year’s 11 finalists to help inform your vote.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://10kdrummachines.com/\">10,000 Drum Machines</a></h2>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https://maxy.world/\">Maxwell Neely-Cohen’s</a> project to collect <a href=\"https://10kdrummachines.com/\">10,000 drum machines</a> is only 0.35% of the way to its goal, but has surprised me so many times with simple, weird, and elegant ideas for what a drum machine can be, using inspiration as diverse as <a href=\"https://10kdrummachines.com/machines/seismic-drum/seismic\">earthquake data</a>, <a href=\"https://10kdrummachines.com/machines/minesweeper/minesweeper\">Minesweeper</a>, the <a href=\"https://10kdrummachines.com/machines/dvdlogo/dvdlogo\">bouncing DVD logo</a>, and <a href=\"https://youtubesequencer.com/\">YouTube samples</a> to turn the web into a musical instrument.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://10kdrummachines.com/\"><img width=\"1024\" height=\"582\" src=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-1-1024x582.png\" srcset=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-1-1024x582.png 1024w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-1-300x170.png 300w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-1-768x436.png 768w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-1-1536x872.png 1536w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-1-800x454.png 800w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-1.png 1722w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://fiftythousandnames.org/\">Fifty Thousand Names</a></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Built on an <a href=\"https://data.techforpalestine.org/\">open dataset</a> of the Palestinian death toll, <a href=\"https://fiftythousandnames.org/\">Fifty Thousand Names</a> is a single page with a stark visualization of 50,000 of the first Palestinians killed in the ongoing Gaza genocide, with names, ages, and birthdays turned into a short sentence or two about each person.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://fiftythousandnames.org/\"><img width=\"1024\" height=\"570\" src=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-2-1024x570.png\" srcset=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-2-1024x570.png 1024w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-2-300x167.png 300w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-2-768x427.png 768w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-2-1536x855.png 1536w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-2-2048x1140.png 2048w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-2-800x445.png 800w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2><br /><a href=\"https://ifeelsomuchsha.me/\">i feel so much shame</a></h2>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https://jackieis.online/\">Jackie Liu’s</a> <a href=\"https://ifeelsomuchsha.me/\">i feel so much shame</a> is an interactive narrative made entirely from scanned Risograph prints, made during her <a href=\"https://www.welcometomyhomepage.net/\">Welcome to my Homepage</a> digital artist residency and published in <a href=\"https://thehtml.review/04/\">The HTML Review’s fourth issue</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://ifeelsomuchsha.me/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"572\" src=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-3-1024x572.png\" srcset=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-3-1024x572.png 1024w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-3-300x168.png 300w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-3-768x429.png 768w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-3-1536x859.png 1536w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-3-2048x1145.png 2048w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-3-800x447.png 800w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2><br /><a href=\"https://consumed.today/\">consumed.today</a></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>A daily digest of the food and media that makes up <a href=\"https://tomato.supply/shen.land/\">Shen’s</a> diet, the minimalist <a href=\"https://consumed.today/\">consumed.today</a> expands into one giant list with photos, links, and chomping sound effects. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://consumed.today/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"522\" src=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-6-1024x522.png\" srcset=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-6-1024x522.png 1024w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-6-300x153.png 300w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-6-768x392.png 768w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-6-1536x783.png 1536w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-6-2048x1044.png 2048w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-6-800x408.png 800w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2><br /><a href=\"https://neal.fun/internet-roadtrip/\">Internet Roadtrip</a></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Every few seconds, everyone currently visiting <a href=\"https://neal.fun/internet-roadtrip/\">Internet Roadtrip</a> votes which direction they want to drive on a Google Street View map, and the most votes wins. (You can also vote to change the radio station or honk the horn, which have both developed their own customs and lore.) That simple idea from <a href=\"https://neal.fun/\">Neal.fun</a>‘s Neal Agarwal spawned a thriving Discord with various factions metagaming the trip and documenting the highlights, touching the physical world in strange and magical ways as they’ve virtually driven from Boston to Newfoundland, with countless detours along the way.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://neal.fun/internet-roadtrip/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"501\" src=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-4-1024x501.png\" srcset=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-4-1024x501.png 1024w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-4-300x147.png 300w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-4-768x375.png 768w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-4-1536x751.png 1536w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-4-2048x1001.png 2048w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-4-800x391.png 800w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2><br /><a href=\"https://nest.oo8.be/\">Nest</a></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Turn on and off music tracks and click and drag the background to create the audio soundscape of <a href=\"https://nest.oo8.be/\">Nest</a>, composed by algorithmic artist/musician <a href=\"https://raphaelbastide.com/\">Raphaël Bastide</a> around a breakbeat MP3 made by the artist Bruno Gola.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://nest.oo8.be/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"644\" src=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-9-1024x644.png\" srcset=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-9-1024x644.png 1024w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-9-300x189.png 300w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-9-768x483.png 768w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-9-1536x966.png 1536w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-9-2048x1288.png 2048w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-9-800x503.png 800w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2><br /><a href=\"https://ellesho.me/\">elle’s homepage</a></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>You can feel the love in every corner of <a href=\"https://ellesho.me/\">Elle’s homepage</a>, from the start screen and isometric pixel art to the clothing changes and built-in source code browser. So many wonderful small touches. (Don’t miss the <a href=\"https://ellesho.me/404\">404 page</a>.)</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://ellesho.me/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"587\" src=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-1024x587.png\" srcset=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-1024x587.png 1024w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-300x172.png 300w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-768x441.png 768w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-1536x881.png 1536w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-2048x1175.png 2048w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-800x459.png 800w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2><br /><a href=\"https://www.trafficcamphotobooth.com/\">Traffic Cam Photobooth</a></h2>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https://wttdotm.com/\">Morry Kolman</a> (aka WTTDOTM) repurposed thousands of New York City’s traffic cameras into selfie cameras with <a href=\"https://www.trafficcamphotobooth.com/\">Traffic Cam Photobooth</a>, raising awareness of public surveillance while earning him huge media attention and a <a href=\"https://www.trafficcamphotobooth.com/assets/CeaseAndDesist.pdf\">cease-and-desist</a> from NYC’s Department of Transportation — which he then <a href=\"https://www.404media.co/traffic-cam-photobooth-cease-and-desist/\">photographed on a traffic cam</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://www.trafficcamphotobooth.com/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"535\" src=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-10-1024x535.png\" srcset=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-10-1024x535.png 1024w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-10-300x157.png 300w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-10-768x402.png 768w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-10-1536x803.png 1536w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-10-2048x1071.png 2048w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-10-800x418.png 800w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2><br /><a href=\"https://cloudgazing.online/\">Cloudgazing</a></h2>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https://cloudgazing.online/\">Cloudgazing</a> is a site where you can draw pictures you see in clouds, share them with others, and see what other people saw in them. (One nice touch: click the play button to see an animation of the original drawing.)</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://cloudgazing.online/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"616\" src=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-8-1024x616.png\" srcset=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-8-1024x616.png 1024w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-8-300x180.png 300w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-8-768x462.png 768w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-8-1536x923.png 1536w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-8-2048x1231.png 2048w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-8-800x481.png 800w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2><br /><a href=\"https://www.historicaltechtree.com/\">Historical Tech Tree</a></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>An audacious project by <a href=\"https://www.hopefulmons.com/\">Étienne Fortier-Dubois</a>, <a href=\"https://www.historicaltechtree.com/\">Historical Tech Tree</a> is an interactive visualization of the entire history of technology and invention, from prehistory to today, with a focus on the connections between technologies.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://www.historicaltechtree.com/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"506\" src=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-7-1024x506.png\" srcset=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-7-1024x506.png 1024w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-7-300x148.png 300w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-7-768x379.png 768w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-7-1536x759.png 1536w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-7-2048x1011.png 2048w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-7-800x395.png 800w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2><br /><a href=\"https://715-999-7483.com/\">715-999-7483</a></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The screenshot below is not what <a href=\"https://715-999-7483.com/\">715-999-7483.com</a> looks like — at least, not anymore. <a href=\"https://brianmoore.com/\">Brian Moore</a> made a website anyone can change with a phone call: just dial the number in the domain, wait until your turn, and say aloud what you want to see on the site. Chaos ensues.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://715-999-7483.com/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"576\" src=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-5-1024x576.png\" srcset=\"https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-5-1024x576.png 1024w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-5-300x169.png 300w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-5-768x432.png 768w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-5-1536x864.png 1536w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-5-2048x1151.png 2048w, https://waxy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/image-5-800x450.png 800w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n\n<p>So much good stuff! </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Go check them all out and <a href=\"https://tinyawards.net/vote/\">vote for your favorite</a> by September 1. I’ll post the winner here when it’s announced.</p>","author":"Andy Baio","siteTitle":"Waxy","siteHash":"35dc61c1bf207cf54e8192cba7836943b040f7b7156ad278540ab82731504f3e","entryHash":"2f8411b5230d487f2903d36e0de700a9b38e8308cb59ae3e625707777134c954","category":"Sites"}